# Required — Red Hat Customer Portal API token
# Get yours at: https://access.redhat.com/management/api
REDHAT_OFFLINE_TOKEN=your_offline_token_here

# AI briefs — powered by Vertex AI (Gemini).
# Pre-configured in the container image — sign in with your @redhat.com Google account
# and AI briefs work automatically. No service account key or project setup needed.
# The shared GCP project `jhorn-pai` has a `domain:redhat.com → Vertex AI User`
# IAM binding, so any @redhat.com OAuth token (with cloud-platform scope) works.
#
# Override only if you want to use your own GCP project instead of the shared one:
GOOGLE_CLOUD_PROJECT=jhorn-pai
# GEMINI_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_KEY=eyJ0eXAi...   (no longer needed for @redhat.com users — only
#                                           supply this if you are NOT on the redhat.com
#                                           domain and lack any other OAuth path)

# Optional — Gemini model and region (defaults shown)
#
# LEAVE THE LOCATION ALONE UNLESS YOU HAVE MEASURED IT. Vertex model
# availability is per-region and the newest models are served from `global`
# first. Measured 2026-10-19 against jhorn-pai with generateContent:
#
#   model                    global   us-east1
#   gemini-3.5-flash (deflt)   200      404
#   gemini-3.1-flash-lite      200      404
#   gemini-2.5-pro             200      200
#   gemini-2.5-flash           200      200
#
# Pinning a region that predates the default model 404s every call, and the
# first thing that says so is a failed generation minutes into a run (#1630).
# The `gemini-model-reachable` startup probe now reports this at boot instead.
# A Gemini default model chosen in Admin → AI Settings → Default Models
# outranks GEMINI_MODEL (and GEMINI_MODEL_LITE), and Admin shows which is in
# effect (#2191). With none chosen there, these decide, then the built-in.
# GEMINI_MODEL=gemini-2.5-flash
# GOOGLE_CLOUD_LOCATION=global

# Optional — Intelligence cache TTLs (BKL-TOKEN-02, tiered)
# Company intelligence changes often (leadership, earnings, M&A) → 14d default.
# Industry analysis is macro-level and stable → 30d default.
# Skip regeneration only fires when BOTH are still fresh.
# INTELLIGENCE_COMPANY_TTL_DAYS=14
# INTELLIGENCE_INDUSTRY_TTL_DAYS=30

# Optional — Google Drive link to shared gcp-oauth.keys.json (shown in setup wizard)
# Most users don't need to change this — the default points to the shared keys file
# VITE_OAUTH_KEYS_DRIVE_URL=https://drive.google.com/file/d/YOUR_FILE_ID/view

# Optional — push notifications via ntfy.sh
# NTFY_TOPIC=asa-command-center

# Optional — server port (default: 7777)
# PORT=7777

# Optional — Salesforce pipeline Google Sheet ID (auto-configured by wizard)
# PIPELINE_FILE_ID=your_sheet_id

# Optional — Tableau Cloud base URL for CCSP session check
# TABLEAU_BASE_URL=https://prod-useast1.online.tableau.com

# Optional — Tableau login email for SSO autofill (auto-fills email field during CCSP scrape login)
# TABLEAU_USER_EMAIL=you@redhat.com

# NODE_ROLE=primary

# Optional — additional territory sheet URLs shown as quick-fill options in the wizard.
# Built-in sheets are pre-loaded automatically; add extras here comma-separated.
# WIZARD_SEED_SHEETS=https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/...

# --- Large installs (150+ accounts) ---
# Uncomment these if you manage more than 150 accounts. setup.sh sets these
# automatically when you answer "yes" to the large install question.
# MEM_LIMIT=16g
# MAX_RSS_MB=12288
# CPU_LIMIT=4

# --- Path overrides (set automatically in container — most users ignore these) ---
# GOOGLE_OAUTH_KEYS=/absolute/path/to/gcp-oauth.keys.json
# GMAIL_TOKEN=/absolute/path/to/.gmail-token.json
# GDRIVE_TOKEN=/absolute/path/to/.gdrive-server-credentials.json

# --- AI provider (optional — leave unset and nothing changes) ---
# Every AI call, POV generation included, goes through one gateway (#1922).
# With 'auto' (the default), calls are answered by Gemini unless a Claude
# backend is configured, in which case Claude answers them. Grounded web
# research (the POV's included) and PDF/image input always stay on Gemini:
# Claude on Vertex has neither.
#
# Nothing here is required. With none of it set you get today's behaviour.
#
# Claude via the Anthropic API — one key, no GCP (get one at console.anthropic.com):
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...
#
# Claude via Vertex AI — needs a GCP project with Anthropic models enabled and
# `gcloud auth application-default login`. No API key:
# CLAUDE_VERTEX_PROJECT=your-gcp-project
# CLAUDE_VERTEX_LOCATION=global
# CLAUDE_MODEL=claude-sonnet-5-5   # default: claude-sonnet-5-5 (set only to override)
# A Claude default model chosen in Admin → AI Settings → Default Models
# outranks CLAUDE_MODEL, and Admin shows which is in effect (#2191).
# Per-call-type models (e.g. Haiku for quick extraction): aiConfig.claudeModelOverrides,
# see docs/guides/claude-model-tiers.md (#1947).
#
# Choose the provider in Admin → AI Settings: the default, and a per-call-type
# override (POV generation is the 'pov-generation' call type). The provider
# saved in Admin wins; AI_PROVIDER is only the default when nothing is saved
# there, and Admin shows which is in effect ("set in Admin" or "default from
# .env"). 'claude' FAILS rather than falling back when nothing above is set.
# AI_PROVIDER=auto               # auto | claude | gemini
#
# POV_GENERATION_PROVIDER is no longer read (#2186): POV generation follows the
# Admin setting like every other call. A POV generation warns if it is still set.
